;;; keys.el -*- lexical-binding: t -*-

;; The Space menu, on Doom Emacs's SPC layout (without Evil; Meow still edits):
;;   SPC SPC  find in project   SPC .  find file     SPC ,  switch buffer
;;   SPC :    command           SPC ;  eval          SPC /  search project
;;   SPC x    scratch           SPC X  capture       SPC u  universal argument
;;   SPC TAB  workspaces        SPC RET bookmarks    SPC `  last buffer
;; with Doom's groups: b buffer, c code, f file, g git, h help, i insert,
;; n notes, o open, p project, q quit, s search, t toggle, w window.
;; Doom leaves these free, so Centaur Emacs's menus keep them:
;;   SPC e  editing: rectangle, multiple cursors, iedit, expand, zap, links
;;   SPC z  folds (kirigami, C-~)       SPC Z  hideshow
;;   SPC d  debugger (dape, M-F5)       SPC M  mode line (C-F6)
;;   SPC A  AI (C-c a)   SPC D  dictionary (C-c d)   SPC T  TODOs (C-c t)
;;   SPC B  browse URL (C-c C-z)        SPC C  consult extras (C-c c)
;; Menus that stayed open as hydras stay open here too (funcs.el). Centaur's
;; own global keys (C-c ..., M-..., F-keys) work as well, in every Meow
;; state. SPC m is the major mode's C-c keys (SPC m c = C-c C-c), SPC \ is Meta
;; (SPC \ x = M-x) and SPC 0-9 a numeric prefix; meow's editing keys are
;; unchanged.

